      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOWILO SIREN (6) sets the standard after beating RUSSIAN MINT at Townsville. He's a track and trip specialist and gets in at featherweight from the inside pillar. A lot to like. SEVENTIES HIT (8) resumes after six months and has the profile to test him, especially with Morrison back aboard after five wins from nine rides on him and a solid track record behind him. HARTSHORN (5) was beaten just under 3L behind SOWILO SIREN last time after early and mid-race bumps, and his previous BM70 fourth reads well enough to give him a genuine chance if he begins cleanly. ALMIGHTY JAB (4) resumes with strong local credentials, a track-and-distance win, and an outstanding Ryan Wiggins record of seven wins from ten rides, though his two runs before the break were more solid than sharp. SPIRIT MEISTER (2) is another one of the dangers and is a home track specialist that has to be considered.",
